{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mass.SLq2LabelParity","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mass.SLq2LabelParity","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Nat.Basic"],"declarations":6,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.SLq2Label.label_admits_even_A","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.SLq2Label.label_admits_even_A","kind":"theorem","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/SLq2LabelParity.lean#L73-L79","doc":"**The atom word admits an `SLq(2)` label exactly at even `A`.** Combining\nSeifert's relation with the measured `μ = A + 1`. Branch-independent: `μ` does\nnot depend on how the `2^(2A+1)` superposition letters resolve. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.SLq2Label.components_odd_iff_even_A","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.SLq2Label.components_odd_iff_even_A","kind":"theorem","line":68,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/SLq2LabelParity.lean#L68-L71","doc":"The measured component count of the atom-word closure, `μ = A + 1`, is odd\nexactly when `A` is even. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.SLq2Label.knot_label_consistent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.SLq2Label.knot_label_consistent","kind":"theorem","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/SLq2LabelParity.lean#L62-L66","doc":"A knot has one component, so the label condition is automatic — which is why\nthe dictionary is stated for knots. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.SLq2Label.seifert_label_parity","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.SLq2Label.seifert_label_parity","kind":"theorem","line":53,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/SLq2LabelParity.lean#L53-L60","doc":"**The label condition is exactly a component-count parity condition.**\nGiven Seifert's relation with `r = n`, the label is consistent iff the closure\nhas an odd number of components. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.SLq2Label.LabelConsistent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.SLq2Label.LabelConsistent","kind":"def","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/SLq2LabelParity.lean#L49-L51","doc":"`D^{N/2}_{w/2,(r+1)/2}` is a genuine irrep index only if `j - m'` is an\ninteger, i.e. `N - r - 1` is even. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.SLq2Label.SeifertRelation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.SLq2Label.SeifertRelation","kind":"def","line":43,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/SLq2LabelParity.lean#L43-L47","doc":"The Euler-characteristic relation for a closed braid on `n` strands with `c`\ncrossings whose closure bounds a genus-`g` Seifert surface with `μ` boundary\ncomponents: `χ = n - c` and `χ = 2 - 2g - μ`. Carried as a hypothesis — it is\nSeifert's algorithm, not something proved here. ","signatureChunk":0}]}